helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	tg	\<emph\>Object\</emph\> variables can store objects of various types, like tables and documents within a document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154807				0	tg	\<emph\>String variables\</emph\> are assigned an empty-string ("") when they are declared.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155072				0	tg	The \<emph\>Option Explicit\</emph\> statement has to be the first line in the module, before the first SUB. Generally, only arrays need to be declared explicitly. All other variables are declared according to the type-declaration character, or - if omitted - as the default type \<emph\>Single\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
