helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"BASCTL_PUSHBUTTON_RID_MACROCHOOSER_RID_PB_ORG\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Macro Organizer\</emph\> dialog, where you can add, edit, or delete existing macro modules, dialogs, and libraries.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01\06130000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124	20			0	tg	To create a new macro, select the "Standard" module in the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>. You can also create a new module, select it in the \<emph\>Macro from \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
