helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3150542				0	tg	Returns a date value from a date string. The date string is a complete date in a single numeric value. You can also use this serial number to determine the difference between two dates.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030102.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	tg	You can use this function to convert a date that occurs between December 1, 1582 and December 31, 9999 into a single integer value. You can then use this value to calculate the difference between two dates. If the date argument lies outside the acceptable range, $[officename] Basic returns an error message.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
