helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3147573				0	tg	Sub ExampleSwitch				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3148522				0	tg	Evaluates a list of arguments, consisting of an expression followed by a value. The Switch function returns a value that is associated with the expression that is passed by this function.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3149579				0	tg	sGender = GetGenderIndex( "John" )				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153346				0	tg	In the following example, the \<emph\>Switch\</emph\> function assigns the appropriate gender to the name that is passed to the function:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	tg	GetGenderIndex = Switch(sName = "Jane", "female", sName = "John", "male")				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	tg	\<emph\>Value:\</emph\> The value that you want to return if the expression is True.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090410.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	tg	MsgBox sGender				2002-02-02 02:02:02
