helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	tg	Many Uno interfaces let you register listeners on a special listener interface. This allows you to listen for specific events and call up the appropriate listener method. The CreateUnoListener function waits for the called listener interface and then passes the interface an object that the interface supports. This object is then passed to the method to register the listener.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
