helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060109.xhp	0	help	par_id3149984				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SVERWEIS\"\>Vertical search with reference to adjacent cells to the right.\</ahelp\> This function checks if a specific value is contained in the first column of an array. The function then returns the value in the same row of the column named by \<emph\>index\</emph\>. If the \<emph\>Sort order\</emph\> parameter is omitted or set to TRUE, it is assumed that the data is sorted in ascending order. In this case, if the exact \<emph\>search criterion\</emph\> is not found, the next value will be returned. If \<emph\>Sort order\</emph\> is set to FALSE or zero, an exact match must be found, otherwise the error \<emph\>Error: Value Not Available\</emph\> will be the result. Thus with a value of zero the data does not need to be sorted in ascending order.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
