helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	tg	You can cancel the Undo command by choosing Edit - Redo.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155504	4			0	tg	If you change the content of a record in a database table that has not been saved, and then use the\<emph\> Undo\</emph\> command, the record is erased.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	tg	The \<emph\>Undo \</emph\>list is cleared when you apply a new layout to a slide.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163803				0	tg	Some commands (for example, editing Styles) cannot be undone.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	tg	To change the number of commands that you can undo, choose Tools - Options - $[officename] - Memory, and enter a new value in the number of steps box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
