helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B81				0	tg	Hidden				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B85				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"svx:TriStateBox:RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS:CB_CHARHIDDEN\"\>Hides the selected characters.\</ahelp\> To display the hidden text, ensure that \<emph\>Non-printing Characters\</emph\> is selected in the \<emph\>View\</emph\> menu. You can also choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Hidden text\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC2				0	tg	To change the color of a text selection, select the text that you want to change, and click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC9				0	tg	If you click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon before you select text, the paint can cursor appears. To change the color of text, select the text with the paint can cursor. To change the color of a single word, double-click in a word. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CD6				0	tg	To undo the last change, right-click.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDA				0	tg	To exit the paint can mode, click once, or press the Escape key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
