helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	tg	You can also apply a shadow effect to borders. For the best results, only apply this effect when all four borders are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3148643				0	tg	If you are in a table or spreadsheet, you can also add or remove predefined borders. Use the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table Bar\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151097				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BORDER\"\>Sets the border options for the selected objects in Writer or Calc.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_MF_LEFT\"\>Enter the distance that you want to have between the left border and the contents of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:LB_LINESTYLE\"\>Click the border style that you want to apply. The border is applied to the borders selected in the preview.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152997				0	tg	To modify the border of an entire table, place the cursor in a table cell, right-click, choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab. To modify the border of a table cell, select the cell, right-click, choose \<emph\>Table\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
