helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	tg	Specify the amount of space that you want to leave between the border and the contents of the selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:LB_LINECOLOR\"\>Select the line color that you want to use for the selected border(s).\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3155351	44			0	tg	You can specify the border position, size, and style. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In $[officename] Writer, you can add borders to pages, frames, graphics, tables, paragraphs, and to embedded objects. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:METRICFIELD:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:ED_SHADOWSIZE\"\>Enter the width of the shadow.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_MF_TOP\"\>Enter the distance that you want to have between the top border and the contents of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3157309				0	tg	Graphics or objects that are anchored to a frame in the document cannot exceed the size of the frame. If you apply a shadow to the borders of an object that fills an entire frame, the size of the object is reduced to display the shadows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_id3158410				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_METRICFIELD_RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER_MF_BOTTOM\"\>Enter the distance that you want to have between the bottom border and the contents of the selection.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BA				0	tg	Merge adjacent line styles				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BE				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"700793922\"\>Merges two different border styles of adjacent cells in a Writer table into one border style.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C1				0	tg	The rules can be condensed to the statement that the stronger attribute wins. If, for example, one cell has a red border of 2 point width, and the adjacent cell has a blue border of 3 point width, then the common border between these two cells will be blue with 3 point width.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
