helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155934				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170802.xhp\" name=\"Table Element Wizard: Field Selection\"\>Table Element Wizard: Field Selection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	par_id3150476				0	tg	Specifies which fields in the table control field should be displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_GW_FIELDSELECTION_LB_SELECTED_FIELDS\"\>Displays the data fields that are accepted into the form field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170802.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Table Element Wizard: Field Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159233				0	tg	\<bookmark_value\>forms; Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154094				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box/List Box Wizard\"\>Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145211				0	tg	You can use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171100.xhp\" name=\"Wizards On/Off\"\>\<emph\>Wizards On/Off\</emph\>\</link\> icon to keep the wizard from starting automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	tg	In the other tables the required field is searched for by using the field names (ControlSource) and then the fields will be completed accordingly. If the field name is not found, the list will remain empty. When list fields contain linked columns, the first column of the other table will be used without a query being shown first.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	tg	In the case of a list box, you select entries from the list, and these are saved in the list table. In the case of a combo box, you can add additional text that can be written to the current database table of the form (values table) and stored there as desired. For this function, the \<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\> has the \<emph\>Data Processing\</emph\> page as the last page, whereas in the case of list boxes this page does not exist. Here you can enter whether and where text that has been entered is to be saved in the values table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150977				0	tg	\<emph\>Combo Boxes\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	tg	If you insert a combo box or a list box in a document, a wizard starts automatically. This wizard allows you to interactively specify which information is shown.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	tg	Combo boxes can display the data of any table. A direct link between the current form table and the table whose values are to be displayed in the combo box (list table) is not required. Combo boxes do not work with references. If the user enters or selects a value and saves it, the value actually displayed will be entered in the form table. As there is no link between the form table and the list table, the \<emph\>Field Link\</emph\> table does not appear here.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	tg	If an article table contains, for example, the number of a supplier, the list box can use the "Supplier number" link to display the name of the supplier from the supplier table. On the \<emph\>Field links\</emph\> page the Wizard will ask you about all the settings required for this link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391				0	tg	The wizards for combo boxes and list boxes differ from each other in their final step. This is because the nature of control fields:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	tg	In the case of combo boxes, users can select one entry from the list entries or enter text themselves. The entries, which are offered as a list from which users can select, may originate from any database table. The entries that users select or enter so that they can be saved can be saved either in the form only, or in a database. If they are saved in a database, they will be written to the database table on which the form is based.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	tg	\<emph\>List Boxes\</emph\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	tg	In the case of a list box, the user selects one entry from a list of entries. These entries are saved in a database table and cannot be modified through the list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	tg	As a general rule, the database table that contains the visible list entries in the form is not the table on which the form is based. The list boxes in a form work by using references; that is, references to the visible list entries are located in the form table (values table) and are also entered as such in the values table if the user selects an entry from the list and saves it. Through reference values, list boxes can display data from a table linked to the current form table. Thus the \<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\> allows two tables of a database to be linked, so that the control field can display a detailed list of a database field that is located in a different table from the one to which the form refers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Combo Box/List Box Wizard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147226				0	tg	Ҷадвал				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170901.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\"\>Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	tg	Specifies a table from the available database tables that contains the data field whose content should be displayed as a list entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	tg	For list boxes, a table that can be linked with the current form table is indicated. The link table must have at least one field in common with the table of the current form. This makes it possible to establish an unambiguous reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	7			0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_TABLE_LB_SELECTTABLE\"\>In the\<emph\> Table \</emph\>field, select the table containing the data field whose content should be displayed in the control field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	tg	For combo boxes, there must be a relationship between the form table and the table containing the data to be displayed in the combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	tg	The table given here appears in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control properties\"\>Control properties\</link\> as an element of an SQL statement in the \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170901.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Combo Box / List Box Wizard: Table Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145669				0	tg	Display Field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153323				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170902.xhp\" name=\"Combo/List Box Wizard: Field Selection\"\>Combo/List Box Wizard: Field Selection\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153894				0	tg	Available Fields				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3093440				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_LISTBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_FIELD_LB_SELECTFIELD\"\>Displays all table fields chosen on the previous Wizard page.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_EDIT_RID_PAGE_LCW_CONTENTSELECTION_FIELD_ET_DISPLAYEDFIELD\"\>Specifies the field whose data are to be shown in the combo or list boxes.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	tg	The field name given here appears in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control properties\"\>Control properties\</link\> as an element of an SQL statement in the \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\> field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	par_id3154228				0	tg	Select the data field specified in the table on previous page, whose contents should be displayed in the list or combo box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170902.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Combo/List Box Wizard: Field Selection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149119				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170903.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard: Field Link\"\>List Box Wizard: Field Link\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	tg	Value table field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827				0	tg	List table field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669				0	tg	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\>, the specified field will appear as entry in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page under \<emph\>Data field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150499				0	tg	The value table is the table of the current form where the list field is inserted. The list table is the table whose data is to be shown in the list field. Both tables must be linked over a mutual data field. These links are to be entered on this page of the Wizard. The field names must not necessarily be the same (this depends upon how the field names are defined in both tables), but both fields must have the same field type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_COMBOBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_FIELDLINK_CMB_VALUELISTFIELD\"\>Specifies the current form data field which should be related to a field in the linked table.\</ahelp\> In addition, click the desired data field in the list field below.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	tg	In \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170102.xhp\" name=\"Control - Properties\"\>Control - Properties\</link\>, the specified field will appear in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of a SQL statement under \<emph\>List Contents\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"DBP_COMBOBOX_RID_PAGE_LCW_FIELDLINK_CMB_TABLEFIELD\"\>Specifies the linked table data field, which is related to the specified value table field.\</ahelp\> In addition, click the data field in the lower list field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	par_id3159224				0	tg	Indicates through which fields tables of values and list tables are linked.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170903.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	List Box Wizard: Field Link				2002-02-02 02:02:02
