helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id273445				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the selected database file for editing.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144740				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DSBrowserExplorer\"\>Turns on and off the view of the data source explorer.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>Explorer On/Off \</emph\>icon is visible on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0212.xhp\" name=\"Database Bar\"\>Table Data bar\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	tg	Роҳбалад Гир./Куш.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	tg	In the data source explorer you see the data sources registered in $[officename] with their links, queries and tables.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151379				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>To rename an entry, call this command and enter the new name.. You can also do this by selecting the entry and pressing F2. The database must support renaming, otherwise this command is not enabled.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153114				0	tg	\<image id=\"img_id3150710\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dsbrowserexplorer.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150710\"\>Тасвир\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Closes the connection to the data source. See \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Connections\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	tg	\<emph\>Establishing a connection\</emph\> - As soon as you select an individual table or query, a connection to the data source is established. Once the connection is opened, the name of the data source, the Queries or Tables entry, and the name of the query or table selected is shown in bold type.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	par_id5943479				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to add/edit/remove a database file from the list of registered databases. The same dialog opens by choosing \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12000000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Роҳбалад Гир./Куш.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Ascending\"\>Sort Ascending\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	5			0	tg	\<variable id=\"dialogsortieren\"\>To sort more than one data field, choose \<emph\>Data - Sort\</emph\>, then choose the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100100.xhp\" name=\"Sort Criteria\"\>Sort Criteria\</link\> tab, where you can combine several sort criteria.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693	2			0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sorts the data of the selected field in ascending order. \</ahelp\> Text fields are sorted alphabetically (A-Z), numerical fields in ascending order (0-9).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380	4			0	tg	\<variable id=\"selektionsortieren\"\>Data of the currently selected field are always sorted. A field is always selected as soon as you place the cursor in the field. To sort within tables, you can also click the corresponding column header.\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	tg	\<image id=\"img_id3147276\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sortascending.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147276\"\>Тасвир\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
