helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	tg	Банизомдарорӣ бо поёнравӣ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149496				0	tg	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sortdescending.png\" id=\"img_id3153255\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153255\"\>Тасвир\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149987	2			0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SortDown\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sorts the data of the selected field in descending order.\</ahelp\> Text fields are sorted alphabetically (Z-A), number fields in numerically descending order (9-0).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Банизомдарорӣ бо поёнравӣ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149495				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12030000.xhp\" name=\"AutoFilter\"\>AutoFilter\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	7			0	tg	To filter with several field names simultaneously, click the \<emph\>Default Filter \</emph\>icon. The \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default Filter dialog\"\>Default Filter\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can combine several filter criteria.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043				0	tg	Автофилтр				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoFilter\"\>Filters the records based on the content of the currently selected data field.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151234				0	tg	\<image id=\"img_id3147261\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfiltered.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147261\"\>Тасвир\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577				0	tg	You can remove the current AutoFilter with the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</link\> icon or with \<emph\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155355				0	tg	Place the cursor in a field name whose content you want to filter and then click the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> icon. Only those records with content identical to the selected field name are visible.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159234				0	tg	For example, to view all the customers from New York, click a field name with the entry "New York". AutoFilter then filters all customers from New York from the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Автофилтр				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155069				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12040000.xhp\" name=\"Remove Filter/Sorting\"\>Remove Filter/Sorting\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	tg	\<image src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_removefilter.png\" id=\"img_id3151315\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151315\"\>Тасвир\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	tg	Remove Filter/Sorting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154094				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RemoveFilterSort\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Cancels the filter settings and displays all of the records in the current table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12040000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Remove Filter/Sorting				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154926				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12050000.xhp\" name=\"Refresh\"\>Refresh\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090				0	tg	Ҷадидсозӣ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	4			0	tg	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Refresh \</emph\>icon to open a submenu with the following commands:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	tg	\<emph\>Rebuild\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\"HID_BROWSER_REFRESH_REBUILDVIEW\"\>Rebuilds the view of the database table. Use this command when you have changed the structure of the table.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147261				0	tg	\<image id=\"img_id3153910\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_reload.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153910\"\>Тасвир\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Refresh\"\>Refreshes the displayed data.\</ahelp\> In a multi-user environment, refreshing the data ensures that it remains current.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	tg	\<emph\>Refresh\</emph\> - Displays the refreshed contents of the database table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Ҷадидсозӣ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	tg	Иловакунии сутунҳои махзани далелҳо				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143284				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaBrwInsert\"\>\<variable id=\"datenintext\"\>Inserts all fields of the marked record into the current document at the cursor position.\</variable\>\</ahelp\> The icon is only visible if the current document is a text document or a spreadsheet.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345	5			0	tg	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In the data source browser, select the records that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon, or drag-and-drop data from the data source browser into the document. This opens the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog. Select whether the data should be inserted as a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070100.xhp\" name=\"table\"\>table\</link\>, as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070200.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> or as \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070300.xhp\" name=\"text\"\>text\</link\>.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	6			0	tg	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The preferences you set in the\<emph\> Insert Database Columns \</emph\>dialog are saved and will be active the next time the dialog is called. This save process is independent of the database and can record the preferences for a maximum of 5 databases.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	tg	Data to Text				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153577	4			0	tg	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>In the data source browser, select the record that you want to insert into the document and then click the \<emph\>Data to Text\</emph\> icon. The record is inserted in the document at the cursor position, with the contents of each individual field of the record copied to a table column. You can also select multiple records and transfer them into the document by clicking the \<emph\>Data to Text \</emph\>icon. Each individual record is then written to a new row.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154186				0	tg	\<image id=\"img_id3147291\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbabrwinsert.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147291\"\>Тасвир\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156326				0	tg	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>If data is inserted into the document as a table, the table properties are not saved along with the data in the document. If you select the \<emph\>AutoFormat\</emph\> function for formatting the table, $[officename] will note the name of the format template. This template will then be used automatically if you insert data as a table again, unless the preferences have been changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Иловакунии сутунҳои махзани далелҳо				2002-02-02 02:02:02
