helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_ALLFIELDS\"\>Searches through all fields.\</ahelp\> If you are running a search in a table, all fields in the table will be searched. If you are running a search in a form, all fields of the logical form (entered under \<emph\>Form\</emph\>) will be searched. If you are running a search in a table control field, all columns that are linked to a valid database table field will be searched.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	tg	Намуна				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127				0	tg	Returns all fields containing the search pattern as an exact match to the contents of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	tg	Cause				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Starts or cancels the search.\</ahelp\> If the search is successfully completed, the corresponding field in the table is highlighted. You can continue the search by clicking the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> button again. You can cancel a search process by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	tg	The \<emph\>State\</emph\> line shows the records returned by the search. If the search reaches the end (or the beginning) of a table, the search is automatically continued at the other end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	tg	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718				0	tg	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORTEXT\"\>Enter the search term in the box or select it from the list.\</ahelp\> The text under the cursor is already copied into the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> combo box. Note that while running a search in a form, tabs and line breaks cannot be processed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	tg	end of field				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	tg	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the beginning of the field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	107			0	tg	The\<emph\> Form \</emph\>combo box is only visible if the current document is a form document with more than one logical form. It does not appear during a search in tables or queries.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518				0	tg	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	tg	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
