helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539	16			0	tg	With the \<emph\>Copy Table \</emph\>dialog you can:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	tg	use the structure of the table as the basis for creating a new table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153147				0	tg	copy the data from the query into another query,				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	2			0	tg	Dragging-and-dropping a query or table opens the \<emph\>Copy Table \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to define the options for copying a query or a table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\05030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	tg	You can copy within the same database or between different databases. Select the query and drag it into the table container of the desired database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
