helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156374	46			0	tg	In the $DBCONFIG$\\Config directory, delete the file that has the same name as the database, for example, " C:\\Adabas\\Sql\\Config\\Big".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156712	47			0	tg	In the $DBWORKS$\\Wrk directory, delete the directory that has the same name as the database., for example "C:\\Adabas\\Sql\\Wrk\\Big".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157869				0	tg	To delete the reference to an Adabas database, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</emph\>. Select the database, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264	94			0	tg	In the $DBCONFIG$ directory, delete the three files that have the same name as the database, but with different extensions. For example, for a database named "Big", delete the "Big.sys", "Big.trs", and "Big.dat" files in the "C:\\Adabas\\".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\30000000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428	88			0	tg	Click \<emph\>Connect to an existing database\</emph\>, and select "Adabas D" in the listbox. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
