helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_id7953733				0	tg	Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\<emph\>- Java\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Class Path\</emph\> button. After you add the path information, restart \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FC				0	tg	\<variable id=\"jdbc\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz02jdbc.xhp\"\>JDBC Connection\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10600				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the options to access a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#jdbc\" name=\"JDBC\"\>JDBC\</link\> database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10623				0	tg	JDBC Examples				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10627				0	tg	\<item type=\"productname\"\>You can use a JDBC driver class to connect to a JDBC database from %PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. The driver class is provided by the database manufacturer. Two examples of JDBC databases are Oracle and MySQL.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062D				0	tg	The driver classes must be added to %PRODUCTNAME in Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Java.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	tg	Oracle database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10638				0	tg	You can use a JDBC driver to access an Oracle database from Solaris or Linux. To access the database from Windows, you need an ODBC driver.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064B				0	tg	On UNIX, ensure that the Oracle database client is installed with JDBC support. The JDBC driver class for the Solaris Oracle client version 8.x is located in the <Oracle client>/product/jdbc/lib/classes111.zip directory. You can also download the latest version of the version from the Oracle web site:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064E				0	tg	http://otn.oracle.com/tech/java/sqlj_jdbc/content.html				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Data source URL\</emph\> box, enter the location of the Oracle database server. The syntax of the URL depends on the database type. See the documentation that came with the JDBC driver for more information. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10668				0	tg	For an Oracle database, the syntax of the URL is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	tg	oracle:thin:@hostname:port:database_name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10674				0	tg	hostname is the name of the machine that runs the Oracle database. You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	tg	port is the port where the Oracle database listens. Ask your database administrator for the correct port address.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067C				0	tg	database_name is the name of the Oracle database. Ask your database administrator for the correct name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067F				0	tg	MySQL database				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	tg	The mm.mysql-2.0.4-bin.jar driver archive for the MySQL database is available on the following web site:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10689				0	tg	The syntax for a MySQL database is:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	tg	mysql://hostname:port/database_name				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10695				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>hostname is the name of the machine that runs the MySQL database.\</ahelp\> You can also replace hostname with the IP address of the server.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	tg	port is the default port for MySQL databases, namely 3306.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabawiz02jdbc.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	tg	database_name is the name of the database.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
