helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menuedit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10580				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Renames the selected object. Depending on the database, some names, characters, and name length might be invalid.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menuedit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058A				0	tg	Кушодан				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menuedit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058E				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the selected object in the last saved state.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menuedit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10591				0	tg	Create as View				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menuedit.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A7				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Converts the selected query to a view. The original query remains in your database file and an additional view is generated on the database server. You must have write permission to add a view to a database.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\menuedit.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AA				0	tg	Most databases use queries to filter or to sort database tables to display records on your computer. Views offer the same functionality as queries, but on the server side. If your database is on a server that supports views, you can use views to filter the records on the server to speed up the display time.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
