helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	tg	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	tg	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	tg	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	tg	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	tg	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
