helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177				0	tg	Setting up Printers				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	tg	Choose a command line that you can use to print on your printer (for example, lp -d my_queue). Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3144503	315			0	tg	You can integrate additional fonts in the $[officename] software. Fonts which you integrate are available exclusively to the $[officename] software and can be used with various Xservers without your having to install them there. To make the fonts available to other programs as well, proceed as usual by adding the fonts to your Xserver. The $[officename] software can display and print out PostScript Type1 fonts as well as TrueType fonts (including TrueType Collections).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145195	330			0	tg	All fonts added to the $[officename] software are listed in the dialog that now appears. Select the fonts you want to delete and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	tg	Select \<emph\>Connect a PDF converter\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	tg	Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	tg	On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "grayscale" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, otherwise choose "color". If switching to grayscale leads to unfavorable results, you can also select "color" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colors are described as well as the PostScript level.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	tg	To make the printer selected from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box the default printer, double-click its name or click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	tg	Assign a name to your new fax printer and determine whether the telephone numbers (see below) marked in the text should be removed from the printout, or not. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776	325			0	tg	In the case of a server installation, the fonts are installed in that installation if possible. If the user has no write access rights, the fonts will be installed in the corresponding user installation so that only the user who installed them can access them.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808				0	tg	Click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	128			0	tg	Some PPD files are installed as default files. If there is no matching PPD file for your printer, you will find various PPD files at http://www.adobe.com/products/printerdrivers/. You can also ask the manufacturer of your printer for PPD files. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	tg	Enter: ./spadmin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	tg	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	tg	Select a printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	tg	When installing a non-PostScript printer, you must set your system so that PostScript can be converted into the language of the printer. We recommend using current PostScript conversion software such as Ghostscript (http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~ghost/).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Selection of drivers\</emph\> list box, select the printer driver you want to install.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	tg	You can now send faxes by printing to the printer that has just been created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	tg	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148419				0	tg	Enter the fax number as text in the document. You can also enter a field that takes the fax number from your active database. In any case, the fax number must start with the characters @@# and end with @@. A valid entry would have the form @@#1234567@@.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	tg	If the printer has more fonts built in than the usual PostScript fonts, you must also load the AFM files for these additional fonts. Copy the AFM files into the {install_path}/share/psprint/fontmetric directory or into the {install_path}/user/psprint/fontmetric directory. You can find AFM files, for example, at ftp://ftp.adobe.com/pub/adobe/type/win/all/afmfiles/.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463				0	tg	If you have installed a fax package such as Efax or HylaFax on your computer, you can send faxes with the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833				0	tg	Select the command on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. You can remove superfluous commands using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148899	333			0	tg	You can also rename fonts added for the $[officename] software. This is especially useful for fonts that contain several localized names.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149072	318			0	tg	Click \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126	321			0	tg	Enter the directory from which you want to add the fonts. Press the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button and select the directory from the path selection dialog or enter the directory directly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	tg	To rename the selected printer, click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>. Enter an appropriate name in the dialog that appears and click OK. The name must be unique and should be chosen so that you can recognize the printer and the application. Printer names must be assigned the same for all users because, when documents are exchanged, the selected printer remains unchanged if the recipient has it under the same name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	347			0	tg	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> to select the directory where you unpacked the PPD files. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	tg	Click \<emph\>Import\</emph\> in the driver selection dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	tg	Following a server installation, the system administrator first logs on as with root privileges, and starts the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>. The administrator then creates a general printer configuration file called {install_path}/share/psprint/psprint.conf for all users. All changes are immediately available to all users.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149590	147			0	tg	On the other hand, when working with spreadsheets and drawings you will be able to use all of the fonts that can be either printed or shown on the screen.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149802	339			0	tg	If you select several fonts to rename, one dialog appears for each selected font.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149909				0	tg	Be sure that you do not delete the generic printer driver, and remember that drivers deleted from server installations are no longer available to other users who are using the same server installation.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	328			0	tg	Start spadmin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	tg	Remember to create one separate print job for each fax, otherwise, the first recipient will receive all the faxes. In the \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge\</emph\> dialog select the \<emph\>Printer\</emph\> option and then select the \<emph\>Single print jobs\</emph\> check box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524				0	tg	In spadmin, click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	tg	The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	tg	Give the printer a name and determine whether it should become the default printer. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787				0	tg	Choose whether to use the default driver or another printer driver. If you are not using the default driver, select the appropriate driver. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826				0	tg	If these characters including the telephone number are not printed, activate the \<emph\>Fax number is removed from the printout\</emph\> option under \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. If no telephone number is entered in the document, a dialog prompting you for it will appear after the printout.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151009	335			0	tg	Click \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151070				0	tg	Select \<emph\>Connect a fax device\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151120	336			0	tg	Select the fonts you want to rename and click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151127	317			0	tg	Enter: ./spadmin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210				0	tg	Select the \<emph\>Create Printer\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	tg	Enter: ./spadmin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151302	327			0	tg	To delete fonts, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	tg	After it starts, the window of the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	tg	Enter: ./spadmin				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152382	145			0	tg	Therefore, only those fonts will be shown in the font selection box when working with a text document which can also be printed, as it is assumed that you will only want to use those fonts that you can actually have printed on paper.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	tg	Assign a name to your new PDF converter. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008	337			0	tg	Enter a new name in the dialog that appears. If the font contains several names, these names will serve as suggestions in the combo box where you enter the new name.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	tg	You can now create PDF documents by printing to the converter that has just been created.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	tg	Select the appropriate driver for your printer. If you are not using a PostScript printer or your model is not listed, use the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> driver or follow the steps below. You can also add new drivers using the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> button or delete unnecessary drivers using the \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153242	331			0	tg	You can delete only the fonts that have been added for the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	tg	Click the \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487	340			0	tg	If you have selected a TrueType Collection (TTC), one dialog appears for each of the fonts contained in it.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822	285			0	tg	The system administrator can also add fonts for all users in the server installation. However, these fonts are available only after restarting the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	144			0	tg	When you are working with the $[officename] software you might notice that a different number of fonts is provided depending on the document type being used. This is because not all of the fonts can be used in every case.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	tg	You should also set the page margins correctly on the \<emph\>Additional settings\</emph\> tab when using the generic printer driver so that your printout is not cropped. You can also enter a description in the Comments field, which will also be displayed on the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	tg	To delete the selected printer, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>. The default printer or a printer that has been created by the system administrator in a server installation cannot be removed using this dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154060	323			0	tg	With the \<emph\>Create soft links only\</emph\> check box you can determine whether the fonts are to be copied into the $[officename] directory or only symbolic links are to be created there. If the fonts to be added are on a data medium that is not always available (such as a CD-ROM), you must copy the fonts.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	tg	In $[officename] you can also activate an icon for sending faxes to a default fax. To do this, choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Toolbars\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> and add from "Documents" the \<emph\>Send Default Fax\</emph\> icon. You can set which fax is used when this button is pressed under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154266	322			0	tg	A list of the fonts from this directory appears. Select the fonts you want to add. To add all the fonts, click \<emph\>Select All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	tg	On the \<emph\>Paper\</emph\> tab page, you can define the paper format and paper tray to be used as the default settings for this printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575				0	tg	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154608	329			0	tg	Click \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154639				0	tg	You should set up the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> in that case. Also make sure that the page margins are set correctly.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	tg	Select the printer driver.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766	334			0	tg	Start spadmin.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	357			0	tg	Go to the {install_path}/program directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154989				0	tg	If a PostScript to PDF converter such as Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is installed on your computer, you can quickly create PDF documents in the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	tg	Enter a command line with which to communicate with the fax in the following dialog. In the command line of each fax sent "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(PHONE)" by the telephone number of the recipient fax machine. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is transmitted in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155118	320			0	tg	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Add Fonts\</emph\> dialog appears.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155128				0	tg	In the next dialog, enter a command line for the PostScript->PDF Converter. Enter the directory where the PDF files should be saved. If you do not provide a directory, the user's home directory will be used. In the command line "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(OUTFILE)" by the target file, the name of which is created from the document name. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the Postscript code is forwarded in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. If Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is in the search path, you can use one of the predefined command lines. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	tg	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	tg	To print a test page, click on \<emph\>Test Page\</emph\>. If the test page fails to print or is incorrectly printed, check all settings as described in \<emph\>Changing Printer Settings\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	tg	Some of these settings can also be set for the current printout in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog or the \<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\> dialog in the $[officename] software with the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155521	338			0	tg	Click OK.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155539	324			0	tg	Click OK. The fonts will now be added.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156174	316			0	tg	To integrate additional fonts in the $[officename] software, proceed as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	tg	In the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>, select the printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog appears containing several tab pages. This is where you can make settings that are used according to the PPD file of the selected printer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156341	319			0	tg	The dialog lists all fonts added for the $[officename] software. You can select and remove fonts using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button or add new fonts with the \<emph\>Add\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	tg	Call the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> as follows:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	tg	Choose whether to use the default driver, the Acrobat Distiller driver or another driver. The driver "Generic Printer (T42 enabled)" prefers the type 42 fonts over type 3 fonts; this driver is a good choice for output to a software PostScript interpreter. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3157982	146			0	tg	In an HTML document or in Web layout, only fonts that are available on screen are offered.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159093	148			0	tg	The $[officename] software tries to match the display on screen to the printout (WYSIWYG = what you see is what you get). Possible problems are shown in the bottom of the dialog \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	tg	If you are using a printer using the PostScript technology, you should install a description file for the printer (PostScript Printer Definition - PPD) so that you can utilize the specific printer features like paper tray selection, duplex print function and all built-in fonts. You can also use the generic printer driver since it contains the most important data and is suitable for most printers. In that case, you will have to do without the paper tray selection and must correctly set the page margins.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	tg	Under UNIX based platforms, the $[officename] software only offers direct support for printers using the PostScript technology. Other printers must be set up as described in the section \<emph\>Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software\</emph\>. The $[officename] software automatically provides a printer with the default driver for each system queue. You can add additional printers as needed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	tg	Under UNIX based platforms, the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> is provided to help you set up printers, faxes and fonts for use with the $[officename] software.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Setting up Printer, Fax and Fonts Under UNIX Based Platforms				2002-02-02 02:02:02
