helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	tg	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	tg	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	tg	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	tg	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	tg	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	tg	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	tg	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	tg	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	tg	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	tg	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	tg	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	tg	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Changing Default Templates				2002-02-02 02:02:02
