helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145147				0	tg	More information is found in the \<emph\>$[officename] Developer's Guide\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	tg	Starts with an empty Calc document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	tg	Creates a temporary copy of \<emph\>{filename}\</emph\> and opens it read-only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3145641				0	tg	-invisible				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146080				0	tg	Starts minimized. The splash screen is not displayed.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146786	46			0	tg	Sets the \<emph\>DISPLAY \</emph\>environment variable on UNIX based platforms to the value \<emph\>{display}\</emph\>. This parameter is only supported by the start script for the $[officename] software on UNIX based platforms.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146928				0	tg	Starts with an empty Math document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009				0	tg	By starting the $[officename] software from the command line you can assign various parameters, with which you can influence the performance. The use of command line parameters is only recommended for experienced users.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147130				0	tg	Notifies the $[officename] software that upon the creation of "UNO Acceptor Threads", a "UNO Accept String" will be used.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147213				0	tg	Starts with an empty Writer document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147341	18			0	tg	When the $[officename] software has been started with this parameter, it can only be ended using the taskmanager (Windows) or the \<emph\>kill \</emph\>command (UNIX based systems).				2002-02-02 02:02:02
