helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	tg	File properties, such as author name, subject, and keywords, help you manage and identify your documents. $[officename] also tracks file statistics, including the number of words and the number of pages in a document, and automatically adds the statistics as part of the file property.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\viewing_file_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	tg	You can view file properties for the current document\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> or for a document in the Windows File Open dialog\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
