helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:convert_to_contour\"\>Converts the selected object to a polygon, or a group of polygons.\</ahelp\> If the conversion creates a group of polygons (for example, when you convert a text object), then press F3 to enter the group before you can select an individual polygon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\01\13050700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601	3			0	tg	Once you convert a line or a text object to a contour, you can no longer edit it as you normally would. Instead, you can edit the contour as you would any polygon, including using the \<emph\>Edit – Points \</emph\>command to adjust its shape.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
