helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	tg	\<variable id=\"line_draw\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/line_draw.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Curves\"\>Кашидани хамидаҳо\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	hd_id46388				0	tg	How to use the Curve tool				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1122165				0	tg	Click where you want the curve to start, and keep holding the mouse button down.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id1556443				0	tg	Do one of the following:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148390				0	tg	Release the mouse where the first control point should be.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868	4			0	tg	The \<emph\>Curve\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150205\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150205\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar opens a toolbar to draw Bézier curves. Bézier curves are defined by a start point and an end point, which are called "anchors". The curvature of the Bézier curve is defined by control points ("handles"). Moving a control point changes the shape of the Bézier curve.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149451				0	tg	Click and drag in any direction to add a smooth anchor point.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	tg	A \<emph\>smooth\</emph\> anchor point may have different line curvatures on either side.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	tg	Bézier curve segments and straight line segments can be joined to form more complex Bézier curves. Three different transitions can be applied to join adjacent segments:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150435				0	tg	A \<emph\>corner\</emph\> anchor point has one or two independent control lines. Changing one side has no effect on the other side.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172	9			0	tg	Double-click on the position of the end point to finish drawing the line. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	tg	Click and release the mouse button to add an anchor point. Move the mouse to draw the next segment.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	tg	A \<emph\>symmetrical\</emph\> anchor point has the same line curvature on either side, and two control lines that move together as a straight line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	22			0	tg	Move the pointer to where you want the curve segment to end. The curve follows the pointer. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155262	5			0	tg	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"img_id3145829\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145829\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Curve\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic1\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezier_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155928	6			0	tg	Click where you want the curve to start, and drag in the direction where you want the curve to go. The control line will indicate the direction. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id4907681				0	tg	On the Drawing toolbar, open the \<emph\>Curves\</emph\> toolbar \<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_linetoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and select the \<emph\>Freeform Line\</emph\>\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_freeline_unfilled.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> tool.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5377056				0	tg	To create a closed shape, double-click the starting point of the line.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_draw.xhp	0	help	par_id5792107				0	tg	Draw the freeform line as you would do with a pencil.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
