helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	tg	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	tg	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	tg	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	tg	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	tg	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	tg	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	tg	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F5\</item\> to run the show.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	tg	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	tg	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	tg	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	tg	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
