helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145230	50			0	tg	For more information about formatting in \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\<emph\> Math\</emph\>, see \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091100.xhp\" name=\"Brackets and Grouping\"\>Brackets and Grouping\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145618				0	tg	Андозабандӣ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3145802	2			0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ATTRIBUTES_CAT\"\>You can choose from various attributes for \<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME\</emph\>\<emph\> Math\</emph\> formulas. Some attributes are displayed in the lower part of the Selection window.\</ahelp\> These attributes are also listed in the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. All attributes not contained in the Selection window or in the context menu must be typed manually in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146071				0	tg	The \<emph\>nbold\</emph\> and \<emph\>nitalic\</emph\> commands remove the bold or italic default fonts of formula components. For example, remove italics from the x in the formula 5 x + 3=28 by typing \<emph\>nitalic\</emph\> before the x as in \<emph\>5 nitalic x + 3=28\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3146322				0	tg	Acute accent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_WIDEVECX\"\>Inserts a wide vector arrow with a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>widevec\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147167				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_CHECKX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with a reverse circumflex ("checkmark") over it.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>check<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147221				0	tg	Нуқта				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147311	57			0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_WIDEHATX\"\>Inserts a wide circumflex ("hat") with a placeholder. \</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>widehat\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	tg	Italic font				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147355				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_ITALX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with italic formatting.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>ital<?>\</emph\> or \<emph\>italic<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147492				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_OVERLINEX\"\>Inserts a line over a placeholder.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>overline<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The line adjusts itself to correct length.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3147621				0	tg	Line over				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148695				0	tg	Note that some entries require spaces for the correct structure. This is especially true when you specify attributes with fixed values instead of placeholders.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3148764				0	tg	Wide circumflex				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149486				0	tg	Line above (bar)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149541				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_DDOTX\"\>Inserts a placeholder with two dots over it.\</ahelp\> You can also directly enter \<emph\>ddot<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149604				0	tg	In describing the following attribute functions, the letter "a" in the icon refers to the placeholder that you would like to assign to the respective attribute. You can substitute this character with any other character that you choose.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	tg	 Use the \<emph\>color\</emph\> command to change the color of your formula. Type \<emph\>color\</emph\>, then type the color name (the available colors are white, black, cyan, magenta, red, blue, green and yellow), then the formula, character or character sequence. The input \<emph\>color green size 20 a\</emph\> results in a green letter "a" with a font size of 20.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149774				0	tg	Шаффоф				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BARX\"\>Inserts a line ("bar") above a placeholder .\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>bar<?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090600.xhp	0	help	par_id3149877				0	tg	Grave accent				2002-02-02 02:02:02
