helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032	17			0	tg	In a master document, targets that are in different sub-documents are not displayed in the\<emph\> Selection\</emph\> list. If you want to insert a reference to the target, you must type the path and the name in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_REF:ED_REFNAME\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\> To set a target, click "Set Reference" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, type a name in this box, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. To reference the new target, click the target name in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159197				0	tg	The advantage of entering a cross-reference as a field is that you do not have to adjust the references manually every time you change the document. Just update the fields with F9 and the references in the document are updated too.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090002.xhp	0	help	par_id3159216				0	tg	If you select text in the document, and then insert a reference, the selected text becomes the contents of the field that you insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
