helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588				0	tg	Displays the number of pages from the "Set page variable" reference point to this field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150696	36			0	tg	In an HTML document, two additional fields are available for the "Set variable" field type: HTML_ON and HTML_OFF. The text that you type in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box is converted to an opening HTML \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tag\"\>tag\</link\> (<Value>) or to a closing HTML (</Value>) tag when the file is saved as an HTML document, depending on the option that you select.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	tg	Тип				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764				0	tg	Variable fields let you add dynamic content to your document. For example, you can use a variable to reset the page numbering.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150996				0	tg	Defines a variable and its value. You can change the value of a variable by clicking in front of the variable field, and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Field\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	tg	The variables are displayed in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> field. When you click the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> button, the dialog\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"Input Field\"\>\<emph\>Input Field\</emph\>\</link\> appears, where you can enter the new value or additional text as a remark.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	tg	Inserts a fixed number, or the result of a formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151377				0	tg	Inserts a custom global variable. You can use the User Field to define a variable for a condition statement. When you change a User Field, all instances of the variable in the document are updated.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	tg	Inserts automatic numbering for tables, graphics, or text frames.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669	9			0	tg	Inserts the current value of the variable that you click in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	tg	Шарҳ				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	tg	Inserts a reference point in the document, after which the page count restarts. Select "on" to enable the reference point, and "off" to disable it. You can also enter an offset to start the page count at a different number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	tg	Show Variable				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154769				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLDVAR_DELETE\"\>Removes the user-defined field from the selection list. You can only remove fields that are not used in the current document.\</ahelp\> To remove a field that is used in the current document from the list, first delete all instances of the field in the document, and then remove it from the list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	tg	Inserts a new value for a variable or a User Field.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155562				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FLDVAR_APPLY\"\>Adds the user-defined field to the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_LB_VARFORMAT\"\>In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, define if the value is inserted as text or a number.\</ahelp\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155982				0	tg	This option is only available if the "Insert formula" field type is selected.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156233				0	tg	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_CB_VARINVISIBLE\"\>Hides the field contents in the document.\</ahelp\> The field is inserted as a thin gray mark in the document. This option is only available for the "Set Variable" and "User Field" field types.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
