helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154506				0	tg	Resizing and Moving Frames, Objects With the Keyboard				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	tg	You can resize and move selected frames and objects with the keyboard.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	tg	To move a selected frame or object, press an arrow key. To move by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	tg	The increment by which you move an object with the keyboard is determined by the document grid. To change the properties of the document grid, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01050100.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Text document - Grid\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04130100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150762				0	tg	To resize a selected frame or object, first press Ctrl+Tab. Now one of the handles blinks to show that it is selected. TO select another handle, press Ctrl+Tab again. Press an arrow key to resize the object by one grid unit. To resize by one pixel, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press an arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
