helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145715				0	tg	When you insert an object, graphic, or frame, an anchor icon appears where the item is anchored. You can position an anchored item by dragging the item to another location. To change the anchoring options of an item, right-click the item, and then choose an option from the \<emph\>Anchor \</emph\>submenu.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3147251				0	tg	You can use anchors to position an object, graphic, or frame in a document. An anchored item remains in place, or moves when you modify the document. The following anchoring options are available:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151181				0	tg	Anchors the selected item as a character in the current text. If the height of the selected item is greater than the current font size, the height of the line containing the item is increased.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	tg	To character				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151235				0	tg	Anchors the selected item to a character.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155071				0	tg	Ба сарсатр				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155094				0	tg	Anchors the selected item to the current paragraph.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155122				0	tg	Ба саҳифа				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\anchor_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155144				0	tg	Anchors the selected item to the current page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
