helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149909				0	tg	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Text Documents\"\>Calculating in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	tg	You can insert a calculation directly into a text document or into a text table.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149972				0	tg	Click in the document where you want to insert the calculation, and then press F2. If you are in a table cell, type an equals sign =.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155547				0	tg	Type the calculation that you want to insert, for example, "=10000/12", and then press Enter.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155565				0	tg	You can also click the \<emph\>Formula \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>, and then choose a function for your formula.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id8316904				0	tg	To reference cells in a Writer text table, enclose the cell address or the cell range in angle brackets. For example, to reference cell A1 from another cell, enter =<A1> into the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Calculating in Text Documents				2002-02-02 02:02:02
