helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147400				0	tg	\<variable id=\"calculate_intable\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intable.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Cell Totals in Tables\"\>Calculating the sum of a series of table cells\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147775				0	tg	Click in the first cell of the series you want to sum up, drag to the final cell, and then release.\<br/\>$[officename] inserts a formula for calculating the sum of the values in the current column.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150507	8			0	tg	Press Enter, or click \<emph\>Apply\</emph\> in the Formula bar. \<br/\>The sum of the values in the current column is entered in the cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150533				0	tg	If you enter a different number anywhere in the column, the sum is updated as soon as you click in the last column cell.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154203				0	tg	Type a number in each cell of the column, but leave the last cell in the column empty.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	tg	Place the cursor in the last cell of the column, and then click the \<emph\>Sum\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table Bar\</emph\>.\<br/\>The\<emph\> Formula Bar\</emph\> appears with the entry "=sum".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Table\</emph\>, and insert a table with one column and more than one row into a text document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intable.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	tg	Similarly, you can also quickly calculate the sum of a row of numbers.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
