helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155541				0	tg	Defining Captions				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145671				0	tg	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, frame, or table. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	tg	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	tg	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption \<emph\>Category\</emph\>. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147765				0	tg	Select the options that you want, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. If you want, you can also enter different text in the \<emph\>Category \</emph\>box, for example "Figure".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	tg	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	tg	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	tg	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	tg	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	tg	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Using Captions 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
