helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert -\</emph\>\<emph\>Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	tg	Click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	tg	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	tg	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	tg	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	tg	Replace the number in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box with 3, and then click\<emph\> Close\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	tg	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert -\</emph\>\<emph\>Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Variables\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	tg	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	tg	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	tg	Type \<emph\>Reminder EQ "3"\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	tg	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	tg	The Format list displays a "General" format after you click Insert.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
