helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	tg	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	tg	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	tg	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose\<emph\> Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles \</emph\>icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	tg	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	tg	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
