helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	tg	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialog. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	tg	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	tg	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	tg	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	tg	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	tg	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	tg	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	tg	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	tg	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	tg	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	tg	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	tg	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or search text in your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	tg	When you have enabled asian language support under \<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialog offers options to search asian text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	tg	Click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	tg	More options				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	tg	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5781426				0	tg	The \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	tg	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	tg	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	tg	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialog without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	tg	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	tg	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	tg	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	tg	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	tg	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	tg	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	tg	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	tg	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for english text.)				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	tg	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	tg	Check \<emph\>Search for Styles\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	tg	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	tg	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a Character Style to all at once.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	tg	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	tg	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	tg	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
