helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	tg	In Writer, you will need different Page Styles. The first Page Style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following Page Style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	tg	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	tg	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	tg	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	tg	Both Page Styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	tg	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between Page Styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	tg	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	tg	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	tg	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	tg	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	tg	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	tg	In the Style list box, select a Page Style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	tg	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" Page Style only, or insert footers to both Page Styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	tg	Double-click the "First Page" style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>. 				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	tg	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	tg	Click into the first page of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	tg	For example, the "First Page" Page Style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press F11 to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> from the context menu. On the Organizer tab, you can see the "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	tg	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	tg	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	tg	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	tg	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the Page Style has a different "next style".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</emph\> or \<emph\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</emph\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current Page Style.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	tg	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	tg	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different Page Style will be applied.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
