helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	tg	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	tg	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	tg	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	tg	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	tg	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	tg	Turning off protection				2002-02-02 02:02:02
