helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	tg	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	tg	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	tg	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	tg	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	tg	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	tg	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	tg	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	tg	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	tg	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	tg	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	tg	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Inserting Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149291				0	tg	\<bookmark_value\>references; modifying cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-references; modifying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>searching;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149291				0	tg	\<variable id=\"references_modify\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references_modify.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Cross-References\"\>Modifying Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	tg	Set the options that you want, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	tg	If you cannot see the field shading of the cross-reference, choose \<emph\>View - Field Shadings\</emph\> or press \<emph\>Ctrl+F8\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3153132				0	tg	Click in front of the cross-reference that you want to modify.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	tg	Use the arrow buttons in the \<emph\>Edit Fields \</emph\>dialog to browse through the cross-references in the current document.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references_modify.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tg	Modifying Cross-References				2002-02-02 02:02:02
