helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	tg	\<image id=\"img_id3149622\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_optimizetable.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153035	33			0	tg	To change the height of a row, place the cursor in a cell in the row, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, and then press the up or the down arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140	13			0	tg	You can resize the width of table cells and columns, as well as change the height of table rows.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364	28			0	tg	To increase the distance from the left edge of the page to the edge of the table, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift, and then press the right arrow key.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891	29			0	tg	You can specify the behavior for the arrow keys by choosing \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</emph\>, and selecting the options that you want in the \<emph\>Keyboard handling\</emph\> area.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
