helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	tg	$[officename] automatically updates the contents of the inserted section whenever the source document is changed. To manually update the contents of the section, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Update All\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	tg	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3148858				0	tg	The contents of the text document are embedded into the current document and are not updated if the source file is changed. If you want the contents to automatically update when you change the source document, insert the file as a link.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	tg	If you want, set the formatting options for the section.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149642				0	tg	In the \<emph\>File Name \</emph\>box, type the name of the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) and locate the file.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149839				0	tg	Locate the text document that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				2002-02-02 02:02:02
